<title>USA: Owens Corning gets Zimbabwe pipe contract.</title>
<headline>Owens Corning gets Zimbabwe pipe contract.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens Corning said Thursday its pipe business segment has been chosen to supply glass-reinforced pipe for the Pungwe to Mutare Water Supply project in Zimbabwe.</p>
<p>Owens Corning A/S, based in Norway and part of Owens Corning's Engineered Pipe Systems business, has been awarded an $18.5 million contract to manufacture and deliver 78 kilometers of 800 milimeter diameter glass-reinforced water transportation pipe over the next 15 months.</p>
<p>The water pipeline will extend from the Pungwe River to Mutare, in eastern Zimbabwe.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
